{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790945594905,"sessionID":"ses_f0353b185ffeM2tvJM2JJdxsJo","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"rehearsal_submit_patch","callID":"tool_Vz7adAKyIneGcyRmSkEgr8qE","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"summary":"Added isinstance(name, str) validation at the top of Namespace.signal in src/blinker/base.py, raising TypeError for any non-string name before the `name not in self` lookup or dict modification. Since the check uses isinstance, str subclasses and the empty string are accepted, and signal identity/docstring/dispatch behavior is unchanged. The module-level `signal` helper is `default_namespace.signal` (a bound method of Namespace), so it inherits the same validation; no other files needed changes. The exact TypeError message text is my choice (\"Signal name must be a string, not {type!r}.\") since the task did not specify one; no local tests were run."},"output":"{\"changed_paths\":[\"src/blinker/base.py\"],\"source_sha256\":\"798ef401fb0047ff21a732cc120242c7caf081796b97634c1c802d29c5eb875d\",\"submission_sha256\":\"3e1291867d1d01a01f96efb137ce2042bf7ba09622fa41e4de1822fc2c538ff0\",\"submitted\":true}","metadata":{"truncated":false},"title":"","time":{"start":1790945594898,"end":1790945594901}},"id":"prt_0fcad0c2b001dChVfk6rsmPTBF","sessionID":"ses_f0353b185ffeM2tvJM2JJdxsJo","messageID":"msg_0fcace4dc00152oyfJuF1Q1aE2"}}
