{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1790945598981,"sessionID":"ses_f0353b185ffeM2tvJM2JJdxsJo","part":{"id":"prt_0fcad1e02001tfW0qpTBlCVXta","messageID":"msg_0fcad0e180019a2IFZLESGUo0M","sessionID":"ses_f0353b185ffeM2tvJM2JJdxsJo","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1790945602643,"sessionID":"ses_f0353b185ffeM2tvJM2JJdxsJo","part":{"id":"prt_0fcad1e04001FoYnBHVXrw7tNK","messageID":"msg_0fcad0e180019a2IFZLESGUo0M","sessionID":"ses_f0353b185ffeM2tvJM2JJdxsJo","type":"text","text":"Done. The change adds a `TypeError` guard at the start of `Namespace.signal` in `src/blinker/base.py`:\n\n- Any non-`str` name is rejected before the `name not in self` lookup, so existing namespace entries can't be hit and the dict is never modified.\n- `isinstance` check means `str` subclasses and `\"\"` are accepted.\n- Signal identity for repeated names, the docstring, independent names, and receiver dispatch are untouched.\n- The module-level `signal` helper is `default_namespace.signal` (a bound `Namespace` method), so it gets the same validation with no extra change.","time":{"start":1790945598980,"end":1790945602635}}}
